<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  TIER 1 — a floating control group standing ON the viewport: the Global
  Toolbar's control capsules, the Tool Rail, the brush controls.

  Translucent and borderless. The model behind a narrow capsule is informative,
  which is why this is the one tier that lets the ground through at all; the
  shape is carried by tone and by the shadow the caller sets alongside it, never
  by an outline. There is no real backdrop blur here and there cannot be — the
  viewport is a SurfaceView and the platform cannot blur what is behind one — so
  "glass" is tone plus opacity plus depth, which is a look the platform keeps.

  A 1 dp HAIRLINE (`UI-CRAFT-R1`). Tone and a soft shadow alone left a
  translucent surface over a rendered model reading as a smudge rather than
  as an edge; the hairline, in the palette's own fsChromeHairline, is what
  every precision tool draws around a floating panel and is what makes the
  surface's corner crisp. It is a hairline and never a frame: 1 dp, at the
  low contrast the role was approved at.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="?attr/fsSurfaceFloating" />
    <corners android:radius="@dimen/radius_capsule" />
    <stroke
        android:width="@dimen/control_border_width"
        android:color="?attr/fsChromeHairline" />
</shape>
